:: Head for the Maze to hide [en Scene3.1] {"position":"1825,750","size":"100,100"}
{
<!-- CHOICE B: Seek shelter in maze
     If player chooses to hide
     Introduces the maze location and first allies -->
(set: $hasUpdatedRules to true)
(set: $dialogs to (a: 
  "We trudged all the way to the entrance of the maze. After making sure it was safe inside, we slipped into a corner and hid—",
  "I remembered the rules: |shake>[out there is not safe right now.]",
  "Fu*k! What the hell is going on out there? And what’s with these stupid fucking rules?",
  "I don’t know... but one thing’s for sure—this is no ordinary place. The only thing I do know is this: if we break their rules, we’ll see each other in hell, just like we promised.",
  "Spit it out! Are you trying to get us killed talking like that?",
  "Weren’t we already asking for death the moment we stepped in here?",
  "Uh… come to think of it, why are there even these rules? It’s so strange.",
  "He asked the very question that had been burning at the back of my mind.",
  "|shake>[Who are “they,” really?]",
  "I gazed across our surroundings. The maze wasn’t just a tangle of branching paths—it was filled with small rooms in between.",
  "(I remembered I read reviews on this maze. Visitors are told to use hints hidden in these rooms to navigate a story, piecing clues together to find the exit.)",
  "(It was similar with the 'escape rooms' trending these days.  drawing and attracting crowds of curious players.)",
  "(However, the maze in front of me had something off from all those visitor reviews.)",
  "The maze was cloaked in a strange, thin mist fog that blurs all the path ahead. Making us pretty much impossible to see where the corridor ended.",
  "Suddenly, a voice drifted out from the far end of the hallway.",
  "|shake>[“Over here—”]",
  "It was a woman’s voice, thin and muffled, as if spoken through a heavy curtain.",
  "The rhythm was wrong—each word spaced too far apart, like the speaker wasn’t entirely familiar with human language.",
  "|shake>[“Come closer—”]",
  "The voice shifted.Now it was a child, trembling, on the verge of crying, the words wet and slurred.",
  "|shake>[“We’re all waiting for you—”]",
  "Another change. A man this time, chuckling under his breath, as if sharing a secret only he found amusing.",
  "All from the same direction, yet each voice belonged to someone different. The transitions came without warning, echoing through the pitch‑black corridor like someone whispering into an empty tin can right beside your ear.",
  "Samuel, terrified beyond reason, was already gripping my hand, ready to take a step toward the voices.",
  "At this moment, I would—"
))


(set: $names to (a: "", "", "Samuel", "Me", "Samuel", "Me", "Samuel", "", "Samuel", "", "", "", "", "", "", "", "","","","","","","","",""))
(set: $step to 1)
(set: $msgName to $names's ($step))
(set: $nextPassage to "none")

(display: "DialogBox")
(display: "Styles")

<audio src="https://cdn.freesound.org/previews/193/193818_2000738-lq.mp3
" autoplay>
}

|choices)[
(button:)[[Close my eyes to drive away the hallucinations->page15.B]]
(button:)[[Follow the Voice Forward->Bad Ending 3]]
]


:: Hollow Smiles and a Brochure [en Scene1.6] {"position":"850,500","size":"100,100"}
{
(set: $dialogs to (a: 
  "The queue was long. It took us nearly twenty minutes to finally reach the entrance. There, the staff stood with identical, mechanical smiles plastered across their faces.",
  "Their professionalism was admirable, yet there was an eerie perfection to it—something I couldn't quite place.",
  "Welcome to the park. Have a pleasant day.",
  "The man in front of us said, his voice as hollow as a recording.",
  "He handed each of us a brochure. I flipped through it, but it was just a collection of mundane safety rules.",
  "(On the surface, it seemed utterly unremarkable.)"
))
(set: $names to (a: "", "", "Staff", "", "", ""))
(set: $step to 1)
(set: $msgName to $names's 1)
(set: $popupImg to "https://i.imgur.com/xjMiha8.png")
(set: $popupTarget to "Rules of the Crimson Tent")
(set: $nextPassage to "none")
