:: page24.B [en Scene5] {"position":"2900,900","size":"100,100"}
{
(set: $dialogs to (a: 
  "We followed the route markers. There were countless branching paths along the way. The maze walls were covered with slurs and insults:",
  "|letter>[“Misfit,” “Weird,” “Difficult,” “Autistic,” “Reclusive,” “Pretentious,” “Weak,” “Trash,” “Useless,” “Unnecessary”… “You should reflect on yourself.”]",
  "Each word felt heavier than the last.",
  "Every intersection had a sign hanging above it: “This is the correct path.” “Everyone takes this way.” “You’ll regret choosing otherwise.” “This is what normal people do.”",
  "But the arrows never pointed in just one direction.",
  "Clara picked up a note identical to the ones from the first room. We leaned in to read it:",
  "//He never fit in. While other children played loudly, he curled up in a corner, lost in his own imagination. He loved quiet. He didn’t want to obey orders.//",
  "//To adults, that was an illness. His parents forced him to be “normal”—forced him to talk, to socialize, to smile. The more he resisted, the more disappointed they became. “Why can’t you be better?”//",
  "//School was hell. He was labeled: freak, lunatic. No one wanted to sit with him. Teachers said, “Why do they only bully you? You should reflect on yourself.”//",
  "//He never did anything wrong. He only wanted to be himself. But society didn’t allow that. Everyone pushed him: be lively, be normal, be like everyone else.//",
  "//No one told him: it’s okay to be different. His world was torn apart, and in the end, he locked himself inside a maze with no exit.//",
  "//And so, the child who loved to imagine… became the monster that creates illusions.//",
  "Mark’s letter continued:",
  "//Now that I’m here, I finally understand the Hallucination’s origin. The “he” in the story… could it be the Hallucination telling his own tale? They were always bound by rules. They hated rules. So they longed to punish the rule‑makers—dragging everyone into the same hell they lived in…//"
))

(set: $names to (a: "", "", "", "", "", "", "", "", "", "", "", "", "", ""))

(set: $step to 1)
(set: $msgName to $names's ($step))
(if: $letter is false)[(set: $nextPassage to "page18.B.1")]
(else:)[(set: $nextPassage to "page 25.B")]
(display: "DialogBox")
(display: "Styles")
}


:: page26.B [en Scene6] {"position":"3200,1150","size":"100,100"}
{
(set: $dialogs to (a: 
  "After opening the door, we finally reached the exit and stepped back onto the main street of the park. What shocked me was how completely it had changed— the place that had been a disaster moments ago, littered with corpses and soaked in blood, was now spotless. Every trace of chaos had vanished as if it had never existed.",
  "What… what is this?",
  "Samuel’s eyes widened, his voice trembling with disbelief. He rubbed his eyes hard, as if trying to force away a hallucination.",
  "There were bodies everywhere. Blood everywhere. How can it all just be—gone?",
  "None of us could respond. We could only stand there in silence, staring at the impossible scene before us."
))

(set: $names to (a: "", "Samuel", "", "Samuel", "", ""))

(set: $step to 1)
(set: $msgName to $names's ($step))
(set: $nextPassage to "page27")

